From 999a63069b871bb88c7f4ec5237007f31011e765 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iamwrm <iamwrm@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 12:18:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 07/17] perf(remote): gather all setup probes in one ssh round
 trip, cache verified path

Attach previously ran 4-5 sequential ssh commands before the bridge could
start (uname, login-shell PATH lookup, known-path scan, per-candidate
version/protocol check, server status). Windows OpenSSH has no
ControlMaster, so each one was a fresh TCP+kex+auth handshake: ~6-9s of
setup at 200ms RTT (i0002 W2).

New src/remote/probe.rs runs a single 'ssh /bin/sh -s' script that emits a
sentinel-tagged blob with all of the above; launcher decision logic is
unchanged and consumes the parsed blob. ensure_remote_server_ready reuses
the probed server status and only falls back to a live round trip when the
probe had no usable status (e.g. fresh install). Happy-path attach drops
from 5+1 to 1+1 ssh connections.

A per-target cache (state_dir()/remote-probe-cache/<target>.json,
disable with HERDR_REMOTE_NO_CACHE=1) remembers the verified binary path
and platform; reattaches probe only that path and skip the login-shell
PATH lookup and uname. Stale cache content falls back to the full probe;
ssh transport errors always propagate.

Install/restart flows keep their existing live probes and prompts.
